{"kind":"report","text":"Approved complete fourth G5a at 34d478544689d9b820fe70cad7ccba59384d2681, tree 44e96bc437c00a4dbfacf1d24eb02f91318f84a4, against Main dba3e76237250b6ce205d511691554de3d809baf. Primary 81bf26cf read first in full. All 83 current artifacts individually inspected for exact path/head and direct promise 79f23cb7 provenance; all 179 exact-path native query results exhausted. Assigned review preparation closes governing request 5aae9b0a. Complete finding set: no remaining required findings.\n\nThe adopted third review b8d8dda2 is addressed. Admission now proves that both the allowed-kind guard and command-open effect execute when the actual commanded device is bound. Their own subjects must be the bound primary transition item or that same device; the kind operand must still name the exact device's fixed kind slot. The optional-unbound guard and optional-unbound effect counterexamples are refused at declaration admission. This is not a claim that those unsafe acts executed and were refused. Checked guard/operand default subjects, unbound-subject skipping, ifPresent validation, transition-only admission, fixed kind, duplicate bindings, and the maintained primary-alert/actual-heater authorize form. Earlier written-order, identical if/unless, targetAt=self, final-before-open and direct kind-guard protections remain intact.\n\nArchitecture: the capability remains one bounded native command/answer mechanism shared by runtime and replay. Command target, independent sensor report and owner outcome retain separate writers. Current versus late answers and exact retries retain their own command identities. Full owner authority comes from retained native installation/genesis and current recorded membership, not a domain field or transport choice. The existing scope-grant preparation path and one-answer reservation remain the appropriate owners. The new correction is a local conservative admission proof; native capability, judges, fold, grants, maintained decl