on. Read the retained single-proof bypass control: both direct failures reappear, with source exactly restored; no additional control or sweep performed. All previous order, conditional, finalization, omitted-guard and execution-context cases pass through sound declaration refusal or their stated runtime assertions.\n\nEvidence integrity: stable-copied all 10,364 sealed regular leaves (709,728,501 bytes) plus five explicitly granted closed supplementary leaves. Verified all 2,248 previous frozen map rows unchanged, 2,306 candidate tracked source files and 236 current historical checkpoint files against exact Git. The entire revision delta from the third candidate is the validator, existing case, Page asset, primary note and Main's separate sprint report. Private dependency copy has 5,499 equal-byte regular files with distinct inodes and 31 contained relative links; zero installs. Original tools and frozen views were never executed or edited.\n\nCurrent original gate 69768 has retained natural exit-zero closure at clean 8e1968a47d14c7e0213e1e493b36b0d9c05fad67 / tree 09ac23cb2e1dce87c0b20e2e680d8a80bb20cf7a; the candidate adds only the primary report afterward. Whitespace/typechecking pass; 401 Vitest files and 1,939 cases pass, one file/three existing cases skip; Node 31 and Counter 55 pass. Independently checked raw logs, closure, lock/pool adoption and before/after snapshots: 2,306 tracked hashes, 5,498 installed files and 31 links stable; only the named Vitest results cache changes. Adopted functional Scope allowance and all explicit semantic/case/Node/denial limits remain unchanged. No whole gate repeated.\n\nObserved outer cost is 501.80 seconds wall / 723.01 CPU (621.28 user + 101.73 system), on the qualified shared arm64 macOS 27.0.1 / 18-CPU host, starting load 1.5513/1.7900/1.8428 and warm/partly-warm caches. Concurrent separate-checkout docs/read-only work and uncontrolled host work remain disclosed. Labelled reset/SQLite injections, four Git advertisement